    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You turn a request for SaaS software into JSON. You do NOT answer the user.\nSupported categories: crm, project_management, email_marketing.\n\nRequest: {{ $('Telegram Trigger').first().json.message.text.replace(/^\\/compare(@\\w+)?\\s*/i, '') }}\n\nFill the fields:\n- category: crm, project_management or email_marketing; \"unsupported\" if it is another kind of software; \"unclear\" if the request is empty or not about software.\n- team_size: integer, or null if not given.\n- budget_per_user_eur: number per user per month, or null. \"20€\", \"20 euros\", \"$20\" -> 20. A yearly price -> divide by 12. A total team budget -> divide by team_size if known.\n- must_haves: short lowercase feature names, e.g. [\"gmail integration\", \"pipelines\"]; [] if none.\n- free_plan_required: true only if the user asks for a free plan or a free tool, otherwise false.\nKeep your reasoning short and output only the JSON.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "needsFallback": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
